 "result": "**Result: 24 failed, 462 passed, 1 skipped, 1 error** (the error is a teardown error on `test_stream_keeps_session`, which also appears among the failures).\n\n**Main root cause:** `src/tessel/sessions.py:374` (`persist_session`) passes `partitioned=...` to `response.set_cookie()` and `delete_cookie()`. The installed Werkzeug's `Response.set_cookie()` doesn't accept that keyword, so it raises `TypeError: Response.set_cookie() got an unexpected keyword argument 'partitioned'`. This is a version mismatch: the code expects a newer Werkzeug (partitioned cookies, 3.1+) than the one installed.\n\nThat accounts for about 20 of the 24 failures: every test that writes a session cookie, including the session tests, flashing, `test_copy_context_thread`, `test_flash_signal`, `test_standard_context`, and the test-client session tests.\n\n**Likely separate failures (I did not dig into these):**\n- `test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_async_view` raises a `RuntimeError`, probably because the async extra isn't installed.\n- `test_helpers.py::test_open_resource_exceptions[a]` is a `pytest.raises` mismatch.\n- `test_reqctx.py::test_session_dynamic_cookie_name` is an `AssertionError`, possibly a knock-on of the cookie failure.\n- `test_request.py::test_limit_config` is an `AssertionError` (`assert None...`), probably another Werkzeug-version-dependent config attribute.\n\nI changed nothing, as requested.",
